"""Alberto Fussar, part A: biography (Origins, Red Dead Redemption 2 chapters 4 and 5, epilogue 1907).

Fussar appears only in Red Dead Redemption 2. Nothing in Red Dead Redemption (1911-1914) or Undead Nightmare mentions
him: no h3 for those periods.

SOURCE REGISTER (fetched Oct 2026; wiki pages cached in scripts/v3/work/_m/, other material in scripts/v3/work/fussar/fc/):
- Red Dead Wiki EN "Alberto Fussar" (scripts/v3/work/fussar/en.txt): History (Background, Saint Denis Chapter, Guarma
  Chapter), Personality, Appearance, Mission appearances, Quotes, Trivia, Gallery captions. Red Dead Wiki FR "Alberto
  Fussar" (fr.txt): Histoire, Interactions, Anecdote.
- Mission pages: "The Gilded Cage" (chapter 4, givers Hosea and Dutch), "Welcome to the New World", "Savagery
  Unleashed" (via the wiki page "Guarma"), "A Kind and Benevolent Despot", "Hell Hath No Fury", "Paradise Mercifully
  Departed" (all chapter 5). The wiki has no "/dialogues" page for any of these missions (Oct 2026).
- TRANSCRIPT: "Red Dead Redemption 2 Full Transcript", Game Scripts Wiki (game-scripts-wiki.blogspot.com), fan
  transcript of the cutscenes and mission dialogue, saved as scripts/v3/work/fussar/fc/gsw.txt (not committed). Scenes
  read in full: "The Gilded Cage" (Bronte on the balcony), "Welcome to the New World" (Levi Simon, Leon Fuentes,
  Hercule Fontaine), "Savagery Unleashed", "A Kind and Benevolent Despot", "Hell Hath No Fury", "Paradise Mercifully
  Departed". Speaker labels are used as given; stage directions (bracketed, fan-written) are used only where a wiki
  page or screenshot agrees.
- Wiki gallery screenshots of the character page, downloaded through the wiki API and viewed (fc/FussarCanon.png,
  fc/FussarStandoff.png, fc/FussarDeath.png): Fussar loading a large wheeled cannon at the top of the tower; Fussar
  aiming a revolver in the cabin; the tower top exploding around the cannon.
- Wiki pages "Guarma", "Aguasdulces", "Cuban Military", "Guarma Rebels", "Levi Simon", "Hercule Fontaine", "Leon
  Fuentes", "JD McKnight".
- Newspapers (wiki article pages, text quoted verbatim): "Guarma Island Sugar Boom" (Blackwater Ledger No. 67, New
  Hanover Gazette No. 32, Saint Denis Times No. 48; published in chapter 4, as in leviticus_B); "Leader of Guarma
  Assassinated" (Blackwater Ledger No. 68, New Hanover Gazette No. 33, Saint Denis Times No. 49); "Unrest in the Tropics"
  (Blackwater Ledger No. 74, New Hanover Gazette No. 39, Saint Denis Times No. 55, the epilogue issue that also carries
  "Bureau of Investigation Founded", as in edgar_A).
- Fact-checked parts aligned with: angelo_A (Bronte names Fussar at the party), leviticus_B (the sugar-boom article),
  arthur_C, dutch_B, javier_A/B/C, bill_A, micah_A/B (Guarma chapter), arthur_E (Fussar among the deaths the story
  imposes on Arthur). HOUSE_FACTS: "Ch. 5, Guarma: Fussar IS killed by Arthur at the cannon."

VERIFIED POINTS
- Bronte points Fussar out on the balcony at the mayor's party and says he owns a sugar plantation on "the island" and
  comes to the city to indulge himself (transcript). In "A Kind and Benevolent Despot" Arthur remembers that Bronte
  pointed him out; Dutch agrees he knew the name (transcript).
- Levi Simon introduces himself as Fussar's "Senior Overseer" and gives the plantation's rank in the Northern Caribbean
  (transcript). Hercule calls him "Colonel Fussar" and Aguasdulces "Fussar's compound" (transcript).
- In Aguasdulces, Fussar questions Javier, who claims to come from Mexico; a soldier punches Javier; Simon is present;
  Fussar later speaks to his men about how America deals with striking workers (transcript; his lines are quoted in
  part B and only paraphrased here).
- Hercule: Fussar knows who the gang are and the price on their heads, and has called in the navy from Cuba (transcript).
  Micah: Fussar holds the ship's captain and has gun positions around the port (transcript).
- Standoff in the cabin, the captain shooting Simon, Fussar firing and running, Dutch missing him (transcript, mission
  page). Fussar at a CANNON in the tower: transcript stage direction ("Fussar loads the cannon"), Hercule's "He's
  shooting", the character page and its gallery screenshot (FussarCanon). The mission page's "Gatling Gun" and the
  Guarma page's "machine gun" are contradicted by the screenshot: not used. Arthur fires a second cannon and destroys the
  top of the tower with Fussar (transcript, character page, HOUSE_FACTS). The mission page's alternative kill by
  gunshot is told in part B (Weapons), not here.
- Fix pass (22 Oct 2026): every newspaper line quoted in part B (sugar-boom detractors, 14-hour shifts, "a great friend
  of America", the obituary's praise) is only paraphrased here (FIX_RULES 3). Added from the transcript: the chaining
  with captured rebels and Simon's order to the corporal ("Welcome to the New World"), Arthur's interrogation and the
  false name Leviticus Cornwall ("Savagery Unleashed"); from the article texts: the sugar-boom headline and US-jobs
  criticism, the obituary's third headline and the Spanish West Indies reaction. Rifle: "kicks" (house wording).

EXCLUDED (one line each)
- Birth in Cuba and service in the Spanish army before 1898 (wiki inference from the medals, sourced to a Reddit post).
- The rank "colonel in the Cuban Military" as a career path ("transferred his allegiance", "rose to the rank"): no source.
- "Anyone opposing him would be tortured and executed": kept only as a Red Dead Wiki claim, next to what the missions show.
- The character page's readings of his character ("open delight", "arrogant and prideful", "pleasure in pain"):
  interpretation; part B owns personality.
- Hercule (and Dutch) drawing Fussar's fire so Arthur can reach the cannon: character page only, no line in the
  transcript (dutch_B dropped it after fact-check); kept as a Red Dead Wiki claim for Hercule only.
- Fussar escaping "through a window" (live v2 page): no source.
- The wiki trivia's reading that Guarma is "even worse" after his death: the 1907 article makes no comparison with Fussar.
- The wiki trivia's parallel with Agustin Allende: interpretation (also dropped in allende_C).
- San Juan Hill being fought on Guarma in the game ("President Congratulates America", Guarma page trivia): about the
  island, not Fussar.
- Dutch's line in "Just a Social Call" that Cornwall's sugar business is destroying the people of Guarma: about Cornwall
  (leviticus fiche), not Fussar.
- The name "Angel" for Arthur's interrogator in "Savagery Unleashed": linked to Fussar only by the wiki page "Cuban
  Military" (part B, Angel entry); the biography says "a soldier".
"""


def two(en, fr): return {"en": en, "fr": fr}


BLOCKS = [
    # ================================================================ Origins
    {"h3": two("Origins", "Origines"), "year": ""},
    {"p": two("The games give no date or place of birth for Alberto Fussar and say nothing of his early life or of how he came to power. By 1899 he governs Guarma, a Caribbean island that [[dutch-van-der-linde|Dutch van der Linde]] places second to the east of Cuba. He holds the rank of colonel. His seat is Aguasdulces, a compound with a sugar factory, guarded by his soldiers.",
              "Les jeux ne donnent ni date ni lieu de naissance pour Alberto Fussar, et ne disent rien de sa jeunesse ni de la façon dont il est arrivé au pouvoir. En 1899, il gouverne Guarma, une île des Caraïbes que [[dutch-van-der-linde|Dutch van der Linde]] situe comme la deuxième à l'est de Cuba. Il a le grade de colonel. Il réside à Aguasdulces, un domaine doté d'une sucrerie et gardé par ses soldats.")},
    {"p": two("Sugar is the island's business. The rebel Leon Fuentes describes the plantation workers as little more than slaves brought in from other islands, worked until they die so that Fussar grows rich. The smuggler [[hercule-fontaine|Hercule Fontaine]] adds that Leon wants the population to rise against Fussar, but that most people are too frightened. The Red Dead Wiki goes further: in its account, the regime tortures and executes its opponents, and the island's rebellion grew out of Fussar's rule.",
              "L'île vit du sucre. Le rebelle Leon Fuentes décrit les ouvriers de la plantation comme de quasi-esclaves amenés d'autres îles, que l'on fait travailler jusqu'à la mort pour enrichir Fussar. Le contrebandier [[hercule-fontaine|Hercule Fontaine]] ajoute que Leon voudrait voir la population se soulever contre Fussar, mais que la plupart des gens ont trop peur. Le Red Dead Wiki va plus loin : à l'en croire, le régime torture et exécute ses opposants, et la rébellion de l'île est née de la manière dont Fussar gouverne.")},
    {"p": two("His sugar sells in the United States. The article \"Guarma Island Sugar Boom\" (Blackwater Ledger No. 67, New Hanover Gazette No. 32, Saint Denis Times No. 48), published in chapter 4, runs under the headline \"FUSSAR CALLED FRIEND THE OF THE US.\" (sic) and the subheading \"CUBAN IMPORTS ON THE RISE\". It describes [[leviticus-cornwall|Leviticus Cornwall]] beside a ship unloading Cuban sugar from Guarma, praising a new era of cooperation between the two countries. Cornwall, the article says, toured sugar plantations in the region twice and signed an exclusive purchase order with the governor, whom he had praised as a friend of America. The paper also gives the critics' view. It says the boom undercuts the American sugar industry and costs American jobs. It reports that Fussar's opponents see him as a controversial and sometimes cruel ruler who runs the island almost like a military post, and that his plantation workers put in very long shifts.",
              "Son sucre se vend aux États-Unis. L'article \"Guarma Island Sugar Boom\" (Blackwater Ledger n° 67, New Hanover Gazette n° 32, Saint Denis Times n° 48), paru au chapitre 4, porte le titre \"FUSSAR CALLED FRIEND THE OF THE US.\" (sic) et le sous-titre \"CUBAN IMPORTS ON THE RISE\" (les importations cubaines en hausse). Il montre [[leviticus-cornwall|Leviticus Cornwall]] devant un navire qui décharge du sucre cubain venu de Guarma, saluant une ère nouvelle de coopération entre les deux pays. D'après le journal, Cornwall a fait deux tournées des plantations de la région et signé une commande d'achat exclusive avec le gouverneur, dont il avait vanté l'amitié envers l'Amérique. Le journal donne aussi la parole aux critiques. Selon lui, cet essor fragilise l'industrie sucrière américaine et coûte des emplois aux États-Unis. Il rapporte que les opposants de Fussar le jugent controversé, parfois cruel, et lui reprochent de diriger l'île presque comme une place militaire, tandis que ses ouvriers enchaînent des journées interminables.")},

    # ================================================================ RDR2 1899
    {"h3": two("Red Dead Redemption 2 (1899)", "Red Dead Redemption 2 (1899)"), "year": "1899"},
    {"h4": two("Chapter 4: Saint Denis", "Chapitre 4 : Saint-Denis"), "chapter": 4},
    {"p": two("Fussar's first appearance is at the garden party given by Mayor Henri Lemieux at his mansion in Saint Denis, in \"The Gilded Cage\". [[angelo-bronte|Angelo Bronte]], who has invited the gang, receives Dutch and [[arthur-morgan|Arthur Morgan]] on a balcony and runs through the guests for them. After the mayor, he picks out Fussar. Bronte says that Fussar owns a sugar plantation on the island and comes to the city to indulge himself, and Dutch laughs with him. Fussar says nothing in the scene. Bronte moves on to Hobart Crawley, to Rains Fall and Eagle Flies, and to the newspaperman Hector Fellowes.",
              "Fussar apparaît pour la première fois à la garden-party que le maire Henri Lemieux donne dans sa demeure de Saint-Denis, dans \"The Gilded Cage\". [[angelo-bronte|Angelo Bronte]], qui a invité la bande, reçoit Dutch et [[arthur-morgan|Arthur Morgan]] sur un balcon et leur passe les invités en revue. Après le maire, il désigne Fussar. Bronte explique que Fussar possède une plantation de sucre sur l'île et qu'il vient en ville pour s'y livrer à la débauche, ce qui fait rire Dutch. Fussar ne prononce pas un mot dans la scène. Bronte passe ensuite à Hobart Crawley, à Rains Fall et Eagle Flies, puis au patron de presse Hector Fellowes.")},
    {"p": two("At the end of chapter 4, after the failed robbery of the Saint Denis bank, Dutch, Arthur, [[micah-bell|Micah Bell]], [[bill-williamson|Bill Williamson]] and [[javier-escuella|Javier Escuella]] escape on a ship that sinks in a storm. The five men wash up on Guarma, Fussar's island.",
              "À la fin du chapitre 4, après l'échec du braquage de la banque de Saint-Denis, Dutch, Arthur, [[micah-bell|Micah Bell]], [[bill-williamson|Bill Williamson]] et [[javier-escuella|Javier Escuella]] s'enfuient sur un navire qui sombre dans une tempête. Les cinq hommes échouent sur Guarma, l'île de Fussar.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 5: Guarma", "Chapitre 5 : Guarma"), "chapter": 5},
    {"p": two("Fussar does not appear in the first Guarma missions. In \"Welcome to the New World\", soldiers led by Levi Simon chain the castaways on the beach together with captured local rebels. Simon presents himself as Fussar's senior overseer and speaks of labor troubles and of Haitian pirates who will soon be hanged in the streets. Dutch gives a false name and Simon promises to free the five men once he knows who they are. In Spanish, he orders a corporal to take them to the jail with the rebels and to shoot them all at the first sign of trouble, then leaves. Hercule Fontaine's rebels ambush the column. Javier is shot in the leg and taken, while the others escape with Hercule, who warns them that Fussar will be desperate to find them. He points out Aguasdulces and the factory where the island's cane is processed.",
              "Fussar n'apparaît pas dans les premières missions de Guarma. Dans \"Welcome to the New World\", des soldats menés par Levi Simon enchaînent les naufragés sur la plage, avec des rebelles de l'île déjà capturés. Simon se présente comme le contremaître principal de Fussar et parle de troubles chez les ouvriers et de pirates haïtiens qui seront bientôt pendus dans les rues. Dutch donne un faux nom, et Simon promet de libérer les cinq hommes dès qu'il saura qui ils sont. En espagnol, il ordonne à un caporal de les conduire en prison avec les rebelles et de tous les abattre au moindre incident, puis s'en va. Les rebelles d'Hercule Fontaine attaquent la colonne. Javier, touché à la jambe, est capturé, tandis que les autres s'enfuient avec Hercule, qui les prévient que Fussar remuera ciel et terre pour les retrouver. Il leur montre Aguasdulces et l'usine où l'on traite la canne de l'île.")},
    {"p": two("Fussar's men are hunting a group of workers who escaped into the jungle the day before. In \"Savagery Unleashed\", Arthur is knocked out by a dart in the jungle and wakes up tied to a chair, where a soldier beats him and demands to know who he is. Arthur gives the false name Leviticus Cornwall, breaks the chair and knocks the soldier out. He and Leon Fuentes then save some of the escaped workers from the gallows.",
              "Les hommes de Fussar traquent un groupe d'ouvriers qui s'est enfui dans la jungle la veille. Dans \"Savagery Unleashed\", Arthur, endormi par une fléchette dans la jungle, se réveille attaché à une chaise ; un soldat le roue de coups pour savoir qui il est. Arthur se fait passer pour Leviticus Cornwall, brise la chaise et assomme le soldat. Avec Leon Fuentes, il sauve ensuite de la potence plusieurs des ouvriers en fuite.")},
    {"p": two("He appears in person in \"A Kind and Benevolent Despot\". On the way through the caves to Aguasdulces, Arthur asks whether Fussar was not one of the men Bronte showed them at the party in Saint Denis, and Dutch agrees that he knew the name. At the top of the ladder, the two men see Fussar arrive with his soldiers and Simon, dragging the captured Javier behind a donkey. Fussar asks Javier who he is; Javier answers that he comes from Mexico and has never met the other men. Fussar mocks him in front of his soldiers, one of whom punches Javier in the face, then leaves him with a parting jibe about Mexicans.",
              "Il apparaît en personne dans \"A Kind and Benevolent Despot\". En chemin vers Aguasdulces, à travers les grottes, Arthur demande si Fussar n'était pas l'un des hommes que Bronte leur a montrés à la réception de Saint-Denis, et Dutch confirme que le nom lui disait quelque chose. En haut de l'échelle, les deux hommes voient arriver Fussar, ses soldats et Simon, qui traînent Javier, prisonnier, derrière un âne. Fussar demande à Javier qui il est ; Javier répond qu'il vient du Mexique et n'a jamais vu les autres hommes. Fussar se moque de lui devant ses soldats, dont l'un frappe Javier au visage, puis le quitte sur une pique au sujet des Mexicains.")},
    {"p": two("While Dutch and Arthur creep around the compound, Fussar can be heard addressing his men in Spanish. He tells them he has just been in America, describes how strikers are dealt with there, and holds it up as the order he wants on Guarma. Meanwhile his soldiers threaten to break Javier's kneecaps to make him talk. Javier keeps repeating that he knows nothing; according to the Red Dead Wiki, he tells them nothing. He is held in a cage. Dutch and Arthur kill the guards inside the refinery, spill the sugar from its sacks and set off the furnace. The building explodes, they take Javier from his cage and fight their way out through the cane fields. Fussar is not seen again in the mission.",
              "Pendant que Dutch et Arthur contournent le domaine, on entend Fussar haranguer ses hommes en espagnol. Il leur raconte qu'il revient d'Amérique, leur décrit le sort qu'on y réserve aux grévistes et présente cet exemple comme l'ordre qu'il veut faire régner à Guarma. Ses soldats, eux, menacent de briser les rotules de Javier pour le faire parler. Javier répète qu'il ne sait rien ; selon le Red Dead Wiki, il ne leur livre aucune information. On le garde dans une cage. Dutch et Arthur éliminent les gardes de la raffinerie, répandent le sucre des sacs et font exploser le four. Le bâtiment saute, ils sortent Javier de sa cage et se frayent un chemin à travers les champs de canne. Fussar ne reparaît plus de la mission.")},
    {"p": two("In \"Hell Hath No Fury\", the gang joins Hercule at the old fort of Cinco Torres. Hercule tells Dutch that Fussar now knows who they are and what price is on their heads. If they can silence him, Hercule says, he can get them away before anyone arrives from America; but Fussar has called in the navy from Cuba, and no boat can leave for now. A warship appears offshore and shells the coast, while soldiers come ashore on the beach below the fort. When one of its shells falls among its own men, Dutch thanks Fussar aloud. Arthur asks how many men Fussar has; Hercule answers that the number does not matter, because Fussar has the money to hire more. Arthur sinks the warship with the fort's cannon, and Hercule announces that a boat is on its way.",
              "Dans \"Hell Hath No Fury\", la bande rejoint Hercule au vieux fort de Cinco Torres. Hercule apprend à Dutch que Fussar sait désormais qui ils sont et quelle prime pèse sur leurs têtes. S'ils parviennent à le faire taire, explique Hercule, il pourra les faire partir avant que quiconque n'arrive d'Amérique ; mais Fussar a fait venir la marine de Cuba, et aucun bateau ne peut quitter l'île pour l'instant. Un navire de guerre surgit au large et bombarde la côte, tandis que des soldats arrivent par la plage, au pied du fort. Quand l'un de ses obus tombe au milieu de ses propres hommes, Dutch remercie Fussar à voix haute. Arthur demande combien d'hommes Fussar a sous ses ordres ; Hercule répond que le nombre n'a pas d'importance, puisque Fussar a de quoi en payer d'autres. Arthur coule le navire avec le canon du fort, et Hercule annonce qu'un bateau est en route.")},
    {"p": two("At the start of \"Paradise Mercifully Departed\", Micah comes back from scouting with bad news: Fussar knows exactly who they are and wants to keep them on the island for a few more days. His men hold the ship's captain, and gun positions cover the harbor so that any boat trying to sail will be shot to pieces. Hercule declares that he will fight Fussar every day he can. Bill stays on the ship with the recovering Javier, while Dutch, Arthur, Micah and Hercule blow up the coastal guns with dynamite and fight their way into Aguasdulces, where the captain is held in a blue building.",
              "Au début de \"Paradise Mercifully Departed\", Micah revient de reconnaissance avec de mauvaises nouvelles : Fussar sait exactement qui ils sont et veut les retenir sur l'île quelques jours de plus. Ses hommes détiennent le capitaine du navire, et des pièces d'artillerie couvrent le port, de sorte que tout bateau qui tenterait de prendre la mer serait criblé d'obus. Hercule déclare qu'il combattra Fussar chaque jour qu'il pourra. Bill reste à bord avec Javier, encore convalescent, tandis que Dutch, Arthur, Micah et Hercule font sauter les canons de la côte à la dynamite et se frayent un chemin jusqu'à Aguasdulces, où le capitaine est retenu dans un bâtiment bleu.")},
    {"p": two("Inside the cabin, Simon is lying in wait; he knocks Arthur to the floor and holds him at gunpoint. Dutch walks in and aims at Simon. Fussar then walks in, revolver drawn, and tells them they are going to die; Dutch draws his second revolver to cover him, and Arthur aims at Fussar from the floor. Fussar warns that the United States Navy is on its way. Dutch answers that this is exactly why Fussar will let them leave, or die where he stands. Arthur kicks a rifle lying on the floor over to the captain, who shoots Simon in the chest and kills him. Fussar fires a few shots and runs out of the cabin; moments later Dutch asks whether he has escaped.",
              "Dans la cabane, Simon attend Arthur ; il le jette à terre et le tient en joue. Dutch entre et braque Simon. Fussar entre alors, revolver au poing, et leur annonce qu'ils vont mourir ; Dutch tire son second revolver pour le tenir en respect, et Arthur, toujours à terre, le met en joue. Fussar prévient que la marine des États-Unis est en route. Dutch répond que c'est justement pour cela que Fussar va les laisser partir, ou mourir sur place. Arthur envoie du pied au capitaine un fusil qui traîne au sol, et le capitaine abat Simon d'une balle en pleine poitrine. Fussar tire quelques coups de feu et s'enfuit de la cabane ; un instant plus tard, Dutch demande s'il s'est échappé.")},
    {"p": two("The group runs for the ship through Fussar's soldiers. Near the port, Hercule spots Fussar at the top of a tower, where he loads a cannon and opens fire on them. Hercule sends Arthur to a second cannon on the ground, further ahead on the left; according to the Red Dead Wiki, Hercule draws Fussar's fire so that Arthur can reach it. Arthur fires at the tower and blows its top apart, killing Fussar. Arthur remarks that he got Fussar for Javier. The captain takes the five gang members on board, Hercule says the rebels will probably disappear back to Haiti, and the ship sails for America. Fussar dies in 1899.",
              "Le groupe court vers le navire à travers les soldats de Fussar. Près du port, Hercule repère Fussar au sommet d'une tour, où il charge un canon et ouvre le feu sur eux. Hercule envoie Arthur vers un second canon, au sol, un peu plus loin sur la gauche ; selon le Red Dead Wiki, Hercule attire sur lui les tirs de Fussar pour permettre à Arthur de l'atteindre. Arthur tire sur la tour et en fait voler le sommet en éclats, tuant Fussar. Arthur lance qu'il a eu Fussar pour Javier. Le capitaine embarque les cinq membres de la bande, Hercule annonce que les rebelles vont sans doute disparaître et repartir en Haïti, et le navire met le cap sur l'Amérique. Fussar meurt en 1899.")},
    {"p": two("Back in the United States, a later issue of the papers (Blackwater Ledger No. 68, New Hanover Gazette No. 33, Saint Denis Times No. 49) carries the article \"Leader of Guarma Assassinated\", headed \"ALBERTO FUSSAR DEAD.\", \"BELOVED LEADER CUT DOWN.\" and \"GREAT SORROW AND SCENES OF RAGE IN GUARMA.\" It reports that the killing caused great excitement on many islands of the Spanish West Indies. It states that \"Reports conflict as to the details of his demise, though early assumptions are that it was part of an attempted coup.\" American business leaders praise him in the article, which also credits him with a particular concern for the women of the island and notes that American firms traded heavily with him in sugar. The killing was first blamed on a revolt of the plantation workers, but \"reports have begun to reach the mainland that several white men were involved in the assassination\", and some blame a band of socialist insurrectionists. Some locals, according to the article, say tensions had grown as working conditions worsened under American pressure for cheaper sugar.",
              "De retour aux États-Unis, un numéro ultérieur des journaux (Blackwater Ledger n° 68, New Hanover Gazette n° 33, Saint Denis Times n° 49) publie l'article \"Leader of Guarma Assassinated\", titré \"ALBERTO FUSSAR DEAD.\" (Alberto Fussar est mort), \"BELOVED LEADER CUT DOWN.\" (un dirigeant bien-aimé abattu) et \"GREAT SORROW AND SCENES OF RAGE IN GUARMA.\" (grande tristesse et scènes de colère à Guarma). Selon le journal, l'assassinat a provoqué une vive agitation dans de nombreuses îles des Antilles espagnoles. On y lit que \"Reports conflict as to the details of his demise, though early assumptions are that it was part of an attempted coup.\" (les récits de sa mort se contredisent, mais les premières hypothèses évoquent une tentative de coup d'État). L'article fait l'éloge du défunt par la voix des milieux d'affaires américains, lui prête une attention particulière au sort des femmes de l'île et rappelle que les entreprises américaines lui achetaient beaucoup de sucre. Le meurtre a d'abord été imputé à une révolte des ouvriers des plantations, mais \"reports have begun to reach the mainland that several white men were involved in the assassination\" (des informations parvenues sur le continent font état de l'implication de plusieurs hommes blancs), et certains accusent une bande d'insurgés socialistes. Des habitants, ajoute l'article, attribuent les tensions à la dégradation des conditions de travail, les importateurs américains exigeant un sucre toujours moins cher.")},

    # ================================================================ Epilogue 1907
    {"h3": two("After his death: the epilogue (1907)", "Après sa mort : l'épilogue (1907)"), "year": "1907"},
    {"p": two("Fussar is mentioned once more in the newspapers of the epilogue period (Blackwater Ledger No. 74, New Hanover Gazette No. 39, Saint Denis Times No. 55). The article \"Unrest in the Tropics\", headed \"COST OF FOOD, FUEL ANGERS CITIZENS.\", describes soaring prices and shortages from Barbados to Cuba. It recalls \"the assassination of prominent sugar industry advocate and Guarman governor Alberto Fussar in 1899\". It reports that, shortly afterwards, American banking institutions, JD McKnight and Co. among them, took control of the sugar industry on several islands, Guarma included. Fields that once fed the islanders were turned over to sugar cane, so that all food has to be imported at great expense. The foreign investors hire locals to guard their plantations, \"subjecting workers to harsh conditions and penalties\". According to the Red Dead Wiki, McKnight's company also took over many of Cornwall's businesses.",
              "Fussar est cité une dernière fois dans les journaux de la période de l'épilogue (Blackwater Ledger n° 74, New Hanover Gazette n° 39, Saint Denis Times n° 55). L'article \"Unrest in the Tropics\", titré \"COST OF FOOD, FUEL ANGERS CITIZENS.\" (le prix de la nourriture et du combustible exaspère la population), décrit l'envolée des prix et les pénuries de la Barbade à Cuba. Il rappelle \"the assassination of prominent sugar industry advocate and Guarman governor Alberto Fussar in 1899\" (l'assassinat en 1899 d'Alberto Fussar, gouverneur de Guarma et ardent défenseur de l'industrie sucrière). Il rapporte que peu après, des établissements bancaires américains, dont JD McKnight and Co., ont pris le contrôle de l'industrie sucrière de plusieurs îles, dont Guarma. Les champs qui nourrissaient les habitants ont été convertis à la canne à sucre, si bien que toute la nourriture doit être importée à grands frais. Les investisseurs étrangers emploient des gens du pays pour garder leurs plantations, \"subjecting workers to harsh conditions and penalties\" (en soumettant les ouvriers à des conditions et à des sanctions sévères). Selon le Red Dead Wiki, la société de McKnight a aussi repris une bonne partie des affaires de Cornwall.")},
]
